1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,695
Rent arrives in a few cheques but is
earned every day.

2
00:00:04,695 --> 00:00:06,403
This tutorial closes September.

3
00:00:06,403 --> 00:00:09,391
As the Accountant, open Omar Haddad's
contract

4
00:00:09,391 --> 00:00:11,952
for R-101 and its recognition schedule.

5
00:00:11,952 --> 00:00:15,366
The rent is 72,000 for 365 days, so

6
00:00:15,366 --> 00:00:18,781
the day rate is 72,000 divided by 365.

7
00:00:18,781 --> 00:00:23,903
Each month is that day rate times its real
number of days:

8
00:00:23,903 --> 00:00:28,599
October's 31 days are 6,115.07, and
February's 28 days are 5,523.29.

9
00:00:28,599 --> 00:00:32,867
September is the last month, so it absorbs
the rounding,

10
00:00:32,867 --> 00:00:36,709
5,917.79, and the schedule adds up to
exactly 72,000.

11
00:00:36,709 --> 00:00:40,977
Every month up to August is Posted, with
its journal.

12
00:00:40,977 --> 00:00:42,684
September is still Planned.

13
00:00:42,684 --> 00:00:44,392
Now open Month-end recognition.

14
00:00:44,392 --> 00:00:47,806
Enter 30 September, the last day of the

15
00:00:47,806 --> 00:00:50,794
month you are closing, and select Preview.

16
00:00:50,794 --> 00:00:52,502
Nothing is written yet.

17
00:00:52,502 --> 00:00:57,197
Nine September periods are waiting,
grouped by building, 52,359.10 in all.

18
00:00:57,197 --> 00:01:01,039
R-202 has two rows: the rent, and a
parking

19
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:04,453
fee that is also earned over the term.

20
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:07,441
Read the total before you post it.

21
00:01:07,441 --> 00:01:09,576
Select Run recognition and confirm.

22
00:01:09,576 --> 00:01:12,563
Each planned period becomes its own
journal,

23
00:01:12,563 --> 00:01:15,551
dated the last day of its month.

24
00:01:15,551 --> 00:01:19,820
Nine journals are posted, each a CIL dated
30 September.

25
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:23,235
Open the General Ledger for September, on
Advance

26
00:01:23,235 --> 00:01:26,222
Rent and Rental Income for the Residences.

27
00:01:26,222 --> 00:01:30,064
Each CIL debits Advance Rent and credits
Rental Income.

28
00:01:30,064 --> 00:01:33,052
Advance Rent falls by 35,112.32, and
Rental

29
00:01:33,052 --> 00:01:36,040
Income rises by exactly the same amount.

30
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:40,735
Back on Omar's contract, September now
shows Posted, with its journal.

31
00:01:40,735 --> 00:01:45,004
Recognition also runs on its own every
night, so closing

32
00:01:45,004 --> 00:01:49,272
a month is mostly a check that nothing is
waiting.
